  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conservation of the Collections at the Madaba Archaeological Museum</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Madaba Archaeological Museum preserves more than 14,000 objects ranging from the Neolithic Period (ca. 10,000 BC) through the end of the Ottoman Period (early 20th century). This project, which is funded by the Cultural Antiquities Task Force, includes storage facility improvements and condition assessments of several objects in the collection.</narrative>
  </description>
